title: Specify the aggregate memory model
status: complete
atomic: true
priority: high
blocked_by: ['8-3']
created_at: '2026-07-29T00:00:00'
updated_at: '2026-07-29T15:00:00'
description: 'Review item 2, decision D1. Write docs/memory-model.md with the rigor of
  docs/access-semantics.md, specifying move-on-assign with compiler-inferred borrows for
  all heap aggregates (Vec, Map, aggregate-containing structs), matching what jinn.md
  already promises. Cover: what ''is'' does for aggregates versus scalars and strings;
  when a read borrows and what ends a borrow; what parameters and return values do to
  ownership; how take and copy fit; interaction with defer, generators, channels, and
  actor message payloads. Rejected: deep value semantics (silent O(n) copy violates the
  performance goal) and today''s shared mutable aliasing (cannot be made safe without GC
  or refcounts). Accept deliberately that ''b is a; b.push(4); log(a.length)'' becomes a
  compile error. This document is the contract 8-6/8-7/8-8 implement against, so write
  it first. DoD: every rule carries a named example; every rejection carries exact
  diagnostic text; the three review section 3 programs appear with required outcomes;
  the ''no reference cycles are constructible'' property is stated as a consequence;
  reviewed against access-semantics.md and escape/mod.rs tiers for contradictions.'
